{"schemaVersion":1,"framework":"agnostic","version":"v0","id":"skills/jf-coding-conventions","title":"jf-coding-conventions","description":"Find the implementation and review rules for JavaScript, TypeScript, and React.","body":[{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[[{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["jf-coding-conventions"]}," provides an implementation and review baseline for JavaScript, TypeScript, and React. The agent reads the target manifest, formatter, compiler configuration, and relevant source before editing, uses installed APIs and configured commands, and preserves existing user changes."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"functions-and-spacing"},"children":["Functions and spacing"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["Top-level functions and React components use ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["function"]}," declarations. A function-valued ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["const"]}," is appropriate for the result of a higher-order function. Callbacks and function-valued props use arrows, except that callbacks defining React components use named functions for identification in React DevTools."]]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["The spacing rules require separation between functions and brace-delimited code blocks, no padding immediately inside braces, and a blank line before a ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["return"]}," that follows another statement in its block. Related declarations stay grouped. Every ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["if"]},", ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["for"]},", and ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["while"]}," body uses braces."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:pre","props":{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark twoslash lsp","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},"tabIndex":"0","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M1.125 0C.502 0 0 .502 0 1.125v21.75C0 23.498.502 24 1.125 24h21.75c.6